ithin him to move the people, emotionally and physically.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:4709860","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["DJ-T Rell"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/4709860-DJ-T-Rell","type":"artist","urls":["https://soundcloud.com/dj-t-rell","https://djt-rell.bandcamp.com","https://www.instagram.com/dj.t.rell/","https://www.youtube.com/itsyaboytrell"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/4726172/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"4726172","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"Okzharp is a producer from South East London who was born in South Africa.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:4726172","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":2028447,"name":"Gervase Gordon"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/4726172-Okzharp","type":"artist","urls":["https://soundcloud.com/okzharp","https://twitter.com/okzharp","https://www.facebook.com/Okzharp/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/556497/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"556497","image":"https://i.discogs.com/QabGzPPb-s8v-BufSmyIayj7OnkEnhMbKThuTMW_0Nc/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:500/w:377/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTU1NjQ5/Ny0xNjIwODgyMTQ4/LTU2MzcuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/RaEqpCgprlKeM8znF283CoVpImXD0aEWS-oJ40nZreo/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTU1NjQ5/Ny0xNjIwODgyMTQ4/LTU2MzcuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Masaki Matsubara (松原正樹, June 27, 1954 – February 8, 2016) was a Japanese guitarist, composer, and arranger born in Takefu (now Echizen City), Fukui Prefecture. Trained at Yamaha's Nemu Music Academy (now Yamaha Music Academy), he moved to Tokyo in the mid-1970s, playing U.S. military base circuits before joining the [a2707574]'s backing band in 1974 and [a1257973]'s [m=2691476] in 1978. His wife was composer and keyboardist [a1147123].\n\nFrom the late 1970s he became one of Japan's most in-demand session guitarists, credited on more than 10,000 recordings across nearly every genre of Japanese popular music. His playing appears on many landmark hits, alongside session and live work for [a404061], [a196513], [a119485], [a5087], [a323464], [a27637], and many others.\n\nIn 1979 he co-founded the pioneering Japanese fusion band [a2840716] (active 1979–1982, later reuniting for shows and tours through 2015). He went on to lead [a5867881] (from 1988) and [a4577758] (from 1986), and co-founded the production unit [a7628468] (1997) with [a1147123]. As a solo artist he released 21 albums beginning with [m=1583869] (1978), including the acclaimed live-oriented HUMARHYTHM series. In 2000 he founded the independent label [l812887]. He died of duodenal cancer in 2016 at age 61.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:556497","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":368517,"name":"K-Project (2)"},{"active":true,"id":1164948,"name":"The Carmets"},{"active":false,"id":1587342,"name":"Nobu Caine"},{"active":true,"id":2840716,"name":"Parachute (7)"},{"active":true,"id":4577758,"name":"Aka-Guy"},{"active":true,"id":5867881,"name":"Triforce (5)"},{"active":true,"id":6830595,"name":"Nobu-Zans"},{"active":true,"id":7168013,"name":"Garp (10)"},{"active":true,"id":7532448,"name":"7 Seven"},{"active":true,"id":7628468,"name":"ON-DO"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["M. Matsubara","M.Matsubara","Masaki","Matsubara","Matsubara Masaki","松原 正樹","松原正樹","松原正樹とるうむセッション"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/556497-Masaki-Matsubara","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.matsubaramasaki.com/","https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E6%9D%BE%E5%8E%9F%E6%AD%A3%E6%A8%B9"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/6047278/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"6047278","image":"https://i.discogs.com/3ahgQJALILd1ESGqOH4wBNGWBQnwDDMXP9l7nGD90Ls/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:400/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTYwNDcy/NzgtMTUxMDMwNTcz/Mi0xMjIyLnBuZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"